# E §5 step 1 under a hole law date (tally 2.3, #247; the lead's P10, H2): `pay` is `at w`, a window; x2
# (known 2026-03-20) states `dd`, which pay's `on` names, so it is in the instance's read set: its
# adjustment's existence is the hole, and so is a count over `adjustments`. Before x2 is known, none; pinned,
# the plain measure. Before: 0 (the law date's hole kept dd's change unseen).
=== m.tally
model b2fm
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-10
  start 2026-03-01
  end 2026-06-30
source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input amt: money PLN
input w: date
input dd: date
move pay: transfers
  on dd
  at w
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt
version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  w = window(2026-03-01, 2026-03-05) "s"
  dd = 2026-03-10 "s"
  amt = 100.00 PLN "s"
  opening[konto] = 500.00 PLN at 2026-03-01 start "s"
version x2
  cite s
  governs 2026-02-01..
  known 2026-03-20
  replace dd = 2026-03-11 "s"
ask n: count(a in adjustments over ..)
ask n_p03: count(a in adjustments over ..) with w = 2026-03-03
ask n_k: count(a in adjustments over ..) as known 2026-03-15
=== expect
n: ?"date within window(2026-03-01, 2026-03-05) not precise enough for the law date of pay" (w)
  unknown day: w
  cut 2026-06-10
n_k: 0
  cut 2026-03-15
n_p03: 0
  cut 2026-06-10
